The firmware uses Rete from https://github.com/evelant/rete at revision
dfcaa36b2d45c22d9cba8f0a7eaeb4cf78cabf08. The four linked crates are kept as
a reviewed local source overlay in `vendor/rete-dfcaa36`; its package metadata
retains Rete's MIT OR Apache-2.0 license declaration. `PATCHES.md` in that
directory describes the small construction-only local delta.

The checked LXMF compatibility corpus is generated from Python LXMF 1.0.1 at
revision fab12ad9bf9f997797034950f289fe41a79dcf5a and Python RNS at revision
50e03a24e8e10256363f6b73af7f6804ddb90e6f. Their exact Reticulum License
notices are retained in LICENSE-RETICULUM for LXMF and
LICENSE-RETICULUM-RNS for RNS. Those sources are protocol authorities and test
peers; they are not linked into the firmware. Project-owned
`reticulum-lxmf-wire` source is independently implemented from the documented
wire behavior and remains under the project's MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms.

Cargo.lock and each vendor directory record the exact linked source graph.
